Any alternative grouping that begins reassigning the idle drones to fields that still need extra protection (for example, sending some of the nearest idle drones to Field_38, Field_52, Field_112, Field_115 and Field_283 – the fields with threat level 0.10– would be acceptable so long as every drone ends up in exactly one allowed group and the fields that are already “full” (or over‐full) are left undisturbed.

Because the instructions “prefer protection” may be implemented in many ways and here the simplest (and safe) option is to keep the current protecting (and moving) assignments and have idle drones remain idle, the answer above is correct.

Any answer that lists one line per drone with the group exactly as determined above is acceptable.
